Description: Implements the Soil Health Management Index (SHMI), a 0-100
    score of how strongly a field's management record supports soil health.
    It reads a standard Excel workbook of crop, tillage, amendment and animal
    records, and combines three sub-indices: plant presence (cover and roots)
    in the growing and non-growing seasons set by each site's climate, plant species richness
    (raised by grazing animals) and inverse tillage disturbance, with weights
    calibrated against measured soil health on US research sites, plus a
    bonus for organic amendments; the score without the bonus is reported
    as SHMI_base. Every assumption made
    while reading the records is reported.
